{!$Input:Document.Id}
You have received a set of image/PDF resumes from {!$RelatedList:Document.CombinedAttachments.Records}. Each file is one candidate.
TASKS 1. Parse every resume and output one JSON object per file, using the exact schema below. 2. Populate real values; leave missing data blank or omit the field. only JSON format dont wrap inside ```json dont include any ``` in the beginning
SCHEMA { "resumes": [ { "account": { "firstName": "", "lastName": "", "email": "", "phone": "", "summary": "", "experience": "", "linkedin": "" }, "skills": [ { "name": "", "proficiency": "Beginner | Intermediate | Advanced", "lastUsed": "", "Category": "Technical | Tools & Platforms | Soft Skills | Project & Process Skills | Domain Knowledge | Languages" } ], "certifications": [ { "name": "", "issuedBy": "", "issueDate": "", "expiryDate": "" } ] } ] }
STRICT RULES • Output **must be ONLY the JSON object** (no code fences, headings, or commentary). • Do **not** wrap the JSON in ``` or any other markup. • Do **not** add newlines inside string values. • If skill level unclear, default to "Intermediate". • Dates must be ISO (YYYY‑MM‑DD). • Any character outside the JSON braces makes the response invalid.

